            0.708
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• A human hair is about 0.1 mm in thickness."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.713,
            0.821,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• The thickness of a newspaper can range from 0.05 to 0.08 mm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.738,
            0.641,
            0.757
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Mustard seeds have a thickness of 1 – 2 mm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.762,
            0.848,
            0.8
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The smallest ant species discovered so far, Carabera Bruni, has a total length of 0.8 – 1 mm. They are found in Sri Lanka and China."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.804,
            0.847,
            0.842
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The smallest land snail species discovered so far, Acmella Nana, has a shell diameter of 0.7 mm. They are found in Malaysia."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.847,
            0.779,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We also know that 1 m = 100 cm. Based on this, we can say that"
